  "date_completed": "2026-06-14",
  "summary": "Hardens Network Worker/Coordinator lifecycle behavior after Codex and Claude review findings, covering fail-closed launch gating, worker URL parity, claim persistence, auth diagnostics, redaction, frontend mode parity, and regression tests.",
  "reason": "Network lifecycle providers were wired, but real-use reliability still depended on consistent worker URL validation, durable claim persistence, clear stale-provider diagnostics, clock-skew auth evidence, strict role/mode handling, and frontend/backend parity.",
  "affected_areas": [
    "command-journal",
    "local-api",
    "network",
    "network-lifecycle",
    "reliability",
    "security",
    "tests",
    "webview"
  ],
  "behavior_before": "Network lifecycle controls could report a safe dry-run for a worker URL that failed at provider startup, claim save failures could still hand work to workers, falsey NetworkRole values could normalize to standalone in launch guards, stale provider diagnostics were generic, auth clock skew looked like token failure, and frontend local-worker mode could display string truth as enabled.",
  "behavior_after": "Network lifecycle launch gating and diagnostics fail closed, worker URL validation/redaction is shared with runtime validation, claims are denied unless in-flight state persists, auth clock skew is diagnosable, frontend mode display follows strict backend booleans, and regression tests cover the hardened paths.",
